46	Firewall Implementation	Advanced interactive simulation for Firewall Implementation - converted from static content	networking2	\N	Intermediate	45	Networking 2	\N	\N	["Master advanced networking concepts", "Configure routing protocols", "Implement network security"]	2	13	t	1	2025-07-25 06:10:40.377204	2025-07-25 06:10:40.40793	[]	\N	[]	[]	0	0	0	0	\N	1	{}	{}	[{"id": 1, "title": "Introduction", "type": "content_review", "description": "Review the fundamental concepts", "content": "\\n            <div class=\\"lesson-content\\">\\n                <h2>Firewall Implementation</h2>\\n                \\n                <div class=\\"lesson-description\\">\\n                    <p>Firewalls are critical security devices that control traffic flow between networks \\n                    based on predefined security rules.</p>\\n                </div>\\n                \\n                <div class=\\"lesson-section\\">\\n                    <h3>Types of Firewalls</h3>\\n                    \\n                    <div class=\\"firewall-types\\">\\n                        <h4>Packet Filtering Firewalls</h4>\\n                        <ul>\\n                            <li>Examine individual packets</li>\\n                            <li>Filter based on IP addresses and ports</li>\\n                            <li>Stateless operation</li>\\n                        </ul>\\n                        \\n                        <h4>Stateful Inspection Firewalls</h4>\\n                        <ul>\\n                            <li>Track connection states</li>\\n                            <li>More sophisticated filtering</li>\\n                            <li>Better security than packet filtering</li>\\n                        </ul>\\n                        \\n                        <h4>Application Layer Firewalls</h4>\\n                        <ul>\\n                            <li>Deep packet inspection</li>\\n                            <li>Application-aware filtering</li>\\n                            <li>Content filtering capabilities</li>\\n                        </ul>\\n                    </div>\\n                </div>\\n                \\n                <div class=\\"lesson-section\\">\\n                    <h3>Firewall Rules and Policies</h3>\\n                    <ul>\\n                        <li>Default deny policy</li>\\n                        <li>Least privilege principle</li>\\n                        <li>Regular rule review and updates</li>\\n                        <li>Logging and monitoring</li>\\n                    </ul>\\n                </div>\\n            </div>\\n            ", "validation": {"type": "acknowledgment", "message": "Click 'Continue' when you've reviewed the content"}, "points": 10}, {"id": 2, "title": "Interactive Learning", "type": "interactive_exercise", "description": "Apply what you've learned", "content": "\\n            <div class=\\"interactive-panel\\">\\n                <h3>Practice Exercise</h3>\\n                <p>Based on the content you just reviewed, complete this interactive exercise.</p>\\n                <div class=\\"exercise-area\\">\\n                    <p>This simulation uses the troubleshoot.html layout with dynamic content.</p>\\n                    <p>Type: Networking 2</p>\\n                </div>\\n            </div>\\n            ", "validation": {"type": "input_validation", "required_inputs": ["understanding"], "correct_answers": ["yes", "completed", "done"], "message": "Enter 'yes' when you understand the concepts"}, "points": 20}, {"id": 3, "title": "Assessment", "type": "knowledge_check", "description": "Validate your understanding", "content": "\\n            <div class=\\"assessment-panel\\">\\n                <h3>Knowledge Check</h3>\\n                <p>Answer the following to complete this simulation:</p>\\n                <div class=\\"question-area\\">\\n                    <p>Rate your understanding of this topic (1-5):</p>\\n                    <input type=\