55	OSPF Configuration	Advanced interactive simulation for OSPF Configuration - converted from static content	networking2	\N	Intermediate	45	Networking 2	\N	\N	["Master advanced networking concepts", "Configure routing protocols", "Implement network security"]	2	22	t	1	2025-07-25 06:10:40.388281	2025-07-25 06:10:40.40793	[]	\N	[]	[]	0	0	0	0	\N	1	{}	{}	[{"id": 1, "title": "Introduction", "type": "content_review", "description": "Review the fundamental concepts", "content": "\\n            <div class=\\"lesson-content\\">\\n                <h2>OSPF Configuration</h2>\\n                \\n                <div class=\\"lesson-description\\">\\n                    <p>Configuring OSPF requires understanding the protocol's hierarchical design \\n                    and proper implementation of areas, networks, and authentication.</p>\\n                </div>\\n                \\n                <div class=\\"lesson-section\\">\\n                    <h3>Basic OSPF Configuration</h3>\\n                    <div class=\\"code-block\\">\\n                        <pre>\\n! Enable OSPF process\\nrouter ospf 1\\n  router-id 1.1.1.1\\n  \\n! Configure networks\\n  network 192.168.1.0 0.0.0.255 area 0\\n  network 10.0.0.0 0.255.255.255 area 1\\n  \\n! Set passive interfaces\\n  passive-interface GigabitEthernet0/1\\n                        </pre>\\n                    </div>\\n                </div>\\n                \\n                <div class=\\"lesson-section\\">\\n                    <h3>OSPF Authentication</h3>\\n                    <div class=\\"code-block\\">\\n                        <pre>\\n! Area authentication\\narea 0 authentication message-digest\\n\\n! Interface authentication\\ninterface GigabitEthernet0/0\\n  ip ospf message-digest-key 1 md5 MyPassword\\n                        </pre>\\n                    </div>\\n                </div>\\n                \\n                <div class=\\"lesson-section\\">\\n                    <h3>Verification Commands</h3>\\n                    <ul>\\n                        <li><code>show ip ospf neighbor</code></li>\\n                        <li><code>show ip ospf database</code></li>\\n                        <li><code>show ip route ospf</code></li>\\n                        <li><code>show ip ospf interface</code></li>\\n                    </ul>\\n                </div>\\n            </div>\\n            ", "validation": {"type": "acknowledgment", "message": "Click 'Continue' when you've reviewed the content"}, "points": 10}, {"id": 2, "title": "Interactive Learning", "type": "interactive_exercise", "description": "Apply what you've learned", "content": "\\n            <div class=\\"interactive-panel\\">\\n                <h3>Practice Exercise</h3>\\n                <p>Based on the content you just reviewed, complete this interactive exercise.</p>\\n                <div class=\\"exercise-area\\">\\n                    <p>This simulation uses the troubleshoot.html layout with dynamic content.</p>\\n                    <p>Type: Networking 2</p>\\n                </div>\\n            </div>\\n            ", "validation": {"type": "input_validation", "required_inputs": ["understanding"], "correct_answers": ["yes", "completed", "done"], "message": "Enter 'yes' when you understand the concepts"}, "points": 20}, {"id": 3, "title": "Assessment", "type": "knowledge_check", "description": "Validate your understanding", "content": "\\n            <div class=\\"assessment-panel\\">\\n                <h3>Knowledge Check</h3>\\n                <p>Answer the following to complete this simulation:</p>\\n                <div class=\\"question-area\\">\\n                    <p>Rate your understanding of this topic (1-5):</p>\\n                    <input type=\\"number\\" id=\\"rating\\" min=\\"1\\" max=\\"5\\" class=\\"form-control\\">\\n                </div>\\n            </div>\\n            ", "validation": {"type": "rating_validation", "min_rating": 3, "message": "Rate your understanding (minimum 3/5