58	Network Diagnostic Tools	Advanced interactive simulation for Network Diagnostic Tools - converted from static content	networking2	\N	Intermediate	45	Networking 2	\N	\N	["Master advanced networking concepts", "Configure routing protocols", "Implement network security"]	2	25	t	1	2025-07-25 06:10:40.391436	2025-07-25 06:10:40.40793	[]	\N	[]	[]	0	0	0	0	\N	1	{}	{}	[{"id": 1, "title": "Introduction", "type": "content_review", "description": "Review the fundamental concepts", "content": "\\n            <div class=\\"lesson-content\\">\\n                <h2>Network Diagnostic Tools</h2>\\n                \\n                <div class=\\"lesson-description\\">\\n                    <p>Various diagnostic tools are available to help identify and resolve \\n                    network issues efficiently and effectively.</p>\\n                </div>\\n                \\n                <div class=\\"lesson-section\\">\\n                    <h3>Command-Line Tools</h3>\\n                    \\n                    <div class=\\"diagnostic-tools\\">\\n                        <h4>Connectivity Testing</h4>\\n                        <ul>\\n                            <li><strong>ping:</strong> ICMP echo requests for basic connectivity</li>\\n                            <li><strong>traceroute:</strong> Path discovery and latency measurement</li>\\n                            <li><strong>pathping:</strong> Combined ping and traceroute functionality</li>\\n                        </ul>\\n                        \\n                        <h4>DNS and Name Resolution</h4>\\n                        <ul>\\n                            <li><strong>nslookup:</strong> DNS query and troubleshooting</li>\\n                            <li><strong>dig:</strong> Advanced DNS lookup tool</li>\\n                            <li><strong>host:</strong> Simple DNS lookup utility</li>\\n                        </ul>\\n                        \\n                        <h4>Network Configuration</h4>\\n                        <ul>\\n                            <li><strong>ipconfig/ifconfig:</strong> Interface configuration</li>\\n                            <li><strong>netstat:</strong> Network connections and statistics</li>\\n                            <li><strong>arp:</strong> ARP table viewing and manipulation</li>\\n                        </ul>\\n                    </div>\\n                </div>\\n                \\n                <div class=\\"lesson-section\\">\\n                    <h3>Advanced Diagnostic Tools</h3>\\n                    <ul>\\n                        <li>Wireshark for packet analysis</li>\\n                        <li>SNMP monitoring tools</li>\\n                        <li>Network scanners (Nmap)</li>\\n                        <li>Bandwidth testing tools (iperf)</li>\\n                        <li>Network mapping utilities</li>\\n                    </ul>\\n                </div>\\n            </div>\\n            ", "validation": {"type": "acknowledgment", "message": "Click 'Continue' when you've reviewed the content"}, "points": 10}, {"id": 2, "title": "Interactive Learning", "type": "interactive_exercise", "description": "Apply what you've learned", "content": "\\n            <div class=\\"interactive-panel\\">\\n                <h3>Practice Exercise</h3>\\n                <p>Based on the content you just reviewed, complete this interactive exercise.</p>\\n                <div class=\\"exercise-area\\">\\n                    <p>This simulation uses the troubleshoot.html layout with dynamic content.</p>\\n                    <p>Type: Networking 2</p>\\n                </div>\\n            </div>\\n            ", "validation": {"type": "input_validation", "required_inputs": ["understanding"], "correct_answers": ["yes", "completed", "done"], "message": "Enter 'yes' when you understand the concepts"}, "points": 20}, {"id": 3, "title": "Assessment", "type": "knowledge_check", "description": "Validate your understanding", "content": "\\n   