59	Common Network Issues	Advanced interactive simulation for Common Network Issues - converted from static content	networking2	\N	Intermediate	45	Networking 2	\N	\N	["Master advanced networking concepts", "Configure routing protocols", "Implement network security"]	2	26	t	1	2025-07-25 06:10:40.392433	2025-07-25 06:10:40.40793	[]	\N	[]	[]	0	0	0	0	\N	1	{}	{}	[{"id": 1, "title": "Introduction", "type": "content_review", "description": "Review the fundamental concepts", "content": "\\n            <div class=\\"lesson-content\\">\\n                <h2>Common Network Issues</h2>\\n                \\n                <div class=\\"lesson-description\\">\\n                    <p>Understanding common network problems and their symptoms helps \\n                    in quick identification and resolution of issues.</p>\\n                </div>\\n                \\n                <div class=\\"lesson-section\\">\\n                    <h3>Physical Layer Issues</h3>\\n                    \\n                    <div class=\\"network-issues\\">\\n                        <h4>Cable Problems</h4>\\n                        <ul>\\n                            <li>Damaged or loose cables</li>\\n                            <li>Incorrect cable types</li>\\n                            <li>Excessive cable length</li>\\n                            <li>Poor cable management</li>\\n                        </ul>\\n                        \\n                        <h4>Hardware Failures</h4>\\n                        <ul>\\n                            <li>Failed network interfaces</li>\\n                            <li>Power supply issues</li>\\n                            <li>Overheating components</li>\\n                            <li>Port malfunctions</li>\\n                        </ul>\\n                    </div>\\n                </div>\\n                \\n                <div class=\\"lesson-section\\">\\n                    <h3>Logical Layer Issues</h3>\\n                    \\n                    <div class=\\"logical-issues\\">\\n                        <h4>Configuration Problems</h4>\\n                        <ul>\\n                            <li>IP address conflicts</li>\\n                            <li>Incorrect subnet masks</li>\\n                            <li>Wrong default gateway</li>\\n                            <li>DNS misconfiguration</li>\\n                        </ul>\\n                        \\n                        <h4>Protocol Issues</h4>\\n                        <ul>\\n                            <li>Routing loops</li>\\n                            <li>VLAN misconfigurations</li>\\n                            <li>Spanning tree problems</li>\\n                            <li>DHCP issues</li>\\n                        </ul>\\n                    </div>\\n                </div>\\n                \\n                <div class=\\"lesson-section\\">\\n                    <h3>Performance Issues</h3>\\n                    <ul>\\n                        <li>Bandwidth saturation</li>\\n                        <li>High latency and jitter</li>\\n                        <li>Packet loss</li>\\n                        <li>Application-specific problems</li>\\n                        <li>Security-related slowdowns</li>\\n                    </ul>\\n                </div>\\n            </div>\\n            ", "validation": {"type": "acknowledgment", "message": "Click 'Continue' when you've reviewed the content"}, "points": 10}, {"id": 2, "title": "Interactive Learning", "type": "interactive_exercise", "description": "Apply what you've learned", "content": "\\n            <div class=\\"interactive-panel\\">\\n                <h3>Practice Exercise</h3>\\n                <p>Based on the content you just reviewed, complete this interactive exercise.</p>\\n                <div class=\\"exercise-area\\">\\n                    <p>This simulation uses the troubleshoot.html layout with dynamic content.</p>\\n                    <p>Type: Networking